DualChannelDacReset|Dual Channel Dac Reset|||||Specifies how the hrtim_dac_reset_trgx trigger is generated
DualChannelDacStep|Dual Channel Dac Step|||||Specifies how the hrtim_dac_step_trgx trigger is generated
DualChannelDacEnable|Dual Channel Dac Enable|||||Enables or not the dual channel DAC triggering mechanism
ReSyncUpdate|Resynchronized Update|Timing Unit||||the update (of registers) coming from adjacent timers or from a software update can now be taken into account either immediately or resynchronized with the timer reset/roll-over event (start of a new counting period)
EventEnableA|Event Counter A Configuration|External Event Counter A||||Enable or Disable the configuration of External Event Counter
EventEnableB|Event Counter B Configuration|External Event Counter B||||Enable or Disable the configuration of External Event Counter
ResetMode|Reset Mode|||||Specifies the External Event Counter Reset Mode.
SourceA|Source|||||Specifies the External Event source selection
SourceB|Source|||||Specifies the External Event source selection
CounterA|Counter|||0|0x3F|Specifies the External Event counter Threshold.
CounterB|Counter|||0|0x3F|Specifies the External Event counter Threshold.
CounterFaultLine|Counter on Faults (Threshold)|||0|15|Specifies the Fault counter Threshold. A fault is considered valid when the number of events is equal to the (FLT5CNT[3:0]+1) value
ResetModeFault|Reset Mode|||||Specifies the reset mode of the fault event counter
BlankingSourceFaultLine1|Blanking Source Type|||||the fault inputs can be temporarily disabled to blank spurious fault events. Specifies the type of blanking source
BlankingSourceFaultLine2|Blanking Source Type|||||the fault inputs can be temporarily disabled to blank spurious fault events. Specifies the type of blanking source
BlankingSourceFaultLine3|Blanking Source Type|||||the fault inputs can be temporarily disabled to blank spurious fault events. Specifies the type of blanking source
